w: ’Tis the Fa- ther’s plea- sure We should call Him Lord,
w: In the Fa- ther’s bo- som With the Spi- rit blest,
w: Thrones and wide do- min- ions, Stars up- on their way,
w: Faith- ful- ly He bore it, Spot- less to the last,
w: To the throne of God- head, To the Fa- ther’s breast;
w: He is God the Sa- vior, He is Christ the Lord,
w: Crown Him as your cap- tain In temp- ta- tion’s hour;
w: For all wreaths of em- pire Meet up- on His brow,
